James inquired about writing a section on the macroeconomic case for adaptation in a report, emphasizing the need for tailored investments that offer significant national benefits and fiscal health. He highlighted the importance of government support in overcoming market failures and the role of resilience investments in addressing systemic risks and achieving national development plans. The discussion included details about a key figure showing sectoral and economy-wide benefit-cost ratios (BCRs) across global regions, revealing that most BCRs are similar, with notable outliers, such as extreme weather adaptation in Sub-Saharan Africa. The overall economy-wide BCR estimate is around 4, based on historical assumptions. A draft section was provided, incorporating these insights and emphasizing the significance of strategic investment and government intervention.
